# Project: Social Media SaaS — Backend
# Stack: Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL, Prisma, BullMQ, Redis
# Scope: Backend only. No frontend files, no HTML, no CSS, no public folder.

## Rules
- This is a backend API project. Never generate frontend code.
- Use industry-standard folder structure for a Node/Express backend.
- All configuration via environment variables. Never hardcode secrets.
- Use async/await throughout. No callbacks.
- Every route must have input validation.
- Error handling must be explicit — no silent catches.
- No emojis, no decorative comments, no vibe-coded patterns.
- Prisma is the only way to interact with the database. No raw SQL unless explicitly asked.
- One concern per file. Routes, controllers, services, middleware are separate.
- Do not install any package that was not explicitly requested.
